  "title": "Kourovka Notebook Problem 21.130",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Conjecture: Let $G$ be a finite additive abelian group with $|G|$ odd. Then any subset $A$ of $G$ with $|A|=n>2$ can be written as $\\{a_1,\\ldots,a_n\\}$ in such a way that all the sums $a_1+a_2,a_2+a_3,\\ldots,a_{n-1}+a_n,a_n+a_1$ are distinct.",
